cases_broadcasts: Each copy of a broadcast opens its own recipient's thread, and a record in that thread holds it. The build before this one (cases_sha256 e0af41fb7c4c5515b901f488b6d960efdc2f2b662b8db6c72d96262c6e8a75f0) kept each broadcast's first copy alone, so 44 records (15 development, 29 held out) lacked the owner's message their thread answers; each now holds that copy as its thread's first text. A broadcast is still one text of the owner, with its first copy's verdict, so every count of counts.json is the same. No other field of a case changed, and no case changed part or split group. The inputs, documents_sha256 and sessions_sha256 are the same.
sessions_read: Every writer session of the dataset, and none is left out, by the owner's answer (dispatch://INFRA-3231/ask/5cfc36a0-1965-46b1-a60e-104869be6c62); export-sessions.sh runs with an empty --exclude. Session text reaches Claude models only (R2). Every text value is masked for secrets before the export (manifest schema infra-3231-session-export/2).
